# Redis users for remote Route to Agent agents (doc/AGENT_INTEGRATION.md).
#
# Copy to agents.acl (git-ignored) and restart manus-redis. One `user` line per agent. Each user can
# only touch its own keys, under manus-agent:<agent_id>:, and only the commands the agent needs.
# `reset` makes the line replace anything the user had before.
#
# Use a SHA-256 hash instead of the clear-text password:
#     printf %s '<redis-password-for-this-agent>' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1
# and put it after the # sign. The agent connects with the clear-text password:
#     MANUS_AGENT_REDIS_URL=redis://agent-<agent_id>:<redis-password-for-this-agent>@<host>:6379/0
#
# user agent-geo-agent reset on #<sha256-of-the-password> ~manus-agent:geo-agent:* +blpop +rpush +hset +expire +del +ping
#
# A line for the user `default` is ignored on purpose (it could remove the app's password).
